# Credentials — never commit
*.p8
*.pem
*.key
rsa_key*
config.toml
.env
.env.*
credentials*

# Snowflake CLI local state
.snowflake/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Temporary exports
tmp/
*.tmp

# Nothing under data/ may ever be ignored.
#
# The patterns above are not exotic and a client delivery could match any of
# them — credentials*, *.key, *.tmp, config.toml, .env.* all describe plausible
# filenames. A delivered file that `git add` silently skips is invisible to
# every integrity check, because both the manifest and the coverage comparison
# derive from the git index: it never reaches Snowflake while CI reports green
# and the documentation asserts the delivery is committed byte-identical.
#
# This negation is the fix. An earlier attempt used a CI step running
# `git ls-files --others --ignored -- data/`, which can never fire: that lists
# untracked files in the working tree, and a fresh CI checkout contains only
# tracked ones — so the check passed unconditionally while the blind spot stayed
# fully open. The property has to hold at the point files are staged, not in CI.
!data/**

